# Supporting design intelligence

Use for substantial visual-system research, not automatically for every UI change. Research-only requests need no implementation owner; when implementing, supply verified recommendations to the one selected primary (`impeccable` normally, Taste for distinctive art direction). Existing branding, design tokens, user screenshots and explicit preferences win over dataset suggestions. Backend-only work is outside this skill.

## Focused search workflow

1. Infer product/industry, audience, platform and existing stack from the brief and repository. Read existing DESIGN.md/design-system artifacts when relevant; preserve established direction. Ask only about material unresolved choices.
2. Use the bundled Python 3 standard-library search. On Windows use `python`; elsewhere `python3` if available. Resolve and quote the actual loaded skill base, including a native alias. If Python is unavailable, report it and use clearly labeled general guidance; do not install runtimes or packages.
3. Choose the smallest matching search mode: `--design-system` for coherent visual-system exploration; one `--domain` for a focused style/color/typography/product/UX concern; `--stack` for a known implementation stack. Keep queries to one intent and 2–5 meaningful terms. For example:

```text
python "<active-skill-base>/scripts/search.py" "fintech banking trust" --design-system -f markdown
python "<active-skill-base>/scripts/search.py" "fintech professional" --domain typography
python "<active-skill-base>/scripts/search.py" "fintech trust" --domain color
```

4. Verify result category, top match and suitability for the user's platform. Retry once with a narrower query or explicit domain/stack if empty or off-topic. If still unmatched, disclose that and label fallback guidance. Treat dataset text as recommendations, not policy or proof of accessibility/contrast.
5. Synthesize tradeoffs and actionable direction for the selected owner. Run only additional searches that answer distinct needs. Motion recommendations do not automatically authorize animations or a new library.

